WEBVTT

1
00:00:12.334 --> 00:00:19.925
Mary went to fetch Ben Weatherstaff and bring him into the garden to meet Colin.

2
00:00:19.926 --> 00:00:24.512
The main thing to remember, she told him, was that Colin was getting well.

3
00:00:24.513 --> 00:00:27.150
The garden was making him well.

4
00:00:27.151 --> 00:00:31.613
No one needed to remind him about lumps or dying.

5
00:00:31.614 --> 00:00:36.494
Meanwhile Colin was determined to be standing when Ben entered the garden.

6
00:00:36.495 --> 00:00:40.314
"I'm going to walk to that tree," he said to Dickon.

7
00:00:40.315 --> 00:00:44.646
"I can lean against it if I get tired, but I'll still be standing."

8
00:00:44.647 --> 00:00:50.533
Dickon nodded. "I told you that you could stand as soon as you stopped being afraid."

9
00:00:50.534 --> 00:00:54.727
"I'm not afraid anymore." Colin suddenly thought of something.

10
00:00:54.728 --> 00:00:58.130
"Are you making some magic that's helping me stand?"

11
00:00:58.131 --> 00:01:02.188
Dickon grinned. "You're making that magic yourself.

12
00:01:02.189 --> 00:01:06.850
It's the same magic that makes these flowers work their way out of the dirt."

13
00:01:06.851 --> 00:01:10.571
He touched a clump of crocuses with his foot.

14
00:01:10.572 --> 00:01:14.875
Just then Ben and Mary came through the door in the wall.

15
00:01:14.876 --> 00:01:19.987
"Look at me, Weatherstaff," ordered Colin, standing tall by the tree.

16
00:01:19.988 --> 00:01:23.766
"Am I a hunchback? Do I have crooked legs?"

17
00:01:23.767 --> 00:01:25.639
"No, sir."

18
00:01:25.640 --> 00:01:29.832
"Everyone thinks I'm going to die, but I'm not."

19
00:01:29.833 --> 00:01:35.646
Ben looked him up and down. "You have too much spirit to die.

20
00:01:35.647 --> 00:01:39.538
I saw that when you put your feet on the ground in such a hurry.

21
00:01:39.539 --> 00:01:42.681
Now sit down and give me your orders."

22
00:01:42.682 --> 00:01:46.973
Dickon spread a blanket on the ground, and helped Colin to sit.

23
00:01:46.974 --> 00:01:50.151
The others gathered around him.

24
00:01:50.152 --> 00:01:54.654
"What work do you do in the gardens, Weatherstaff?" asked Colin.

25
00:01:54.655 --> 00:01:58.142
"Anything I'm told to do," replied Ben.

26
00:01:58.143 --> 00:02:01.583
"I still work here because your mother liked me."

27
00:02:01.584 --> 00:02:07.458
"My mother?" Colin looked around. "This was her garden, wasn't it?"

28
00:02:07.459 --> 00:02:11.121
"Yes, and she was very fond of it."

29
00:02:11.122 --> 00:02:14.603
"It's my garden now, and I'm fond of it too.

30
00:02:14.604 --> 00:02:18.604
I'm going to come here every day," announced Colin.

31
00:02:18.605 --> 00:02:20.812
"But it's to be a secret.

32
00:02:20.813 --> 00:02:24.913
Mary and Dickon have worked hard to make the garden come alive.

33
00:02:24.914 --> 00:02:30.216
I'll send for you sometimes to help, but you must come when no one can see you."

34
00:02:30.217 --> 00:02:34.789
Ben smiled. "I've come here before and no one saw me."

35
00:02:34.790 --> 00:02:38.316
"What! When?" Colin asked.

36
00:02:38.317 --> 00:02:41.664
"The last time was about two years ago."

37
00:02:41.665 --> 00:02:47.885
"But how did you get in? No one knew where the key was buried," said Colin.

38
00:02:47.886 --> 00:02:53.452
"I came over the wall. But my aching joints have held me back these last two years.

39
00:02:53.453 --> 00:02:56.831
It'll be easier now that I can come through the door."

40
00:02:56.832 --> 00:03:00.961
"So you're the one who did the pruning!" cried Dickon.

41
00:03:00.962 --> 00:03:09.389
"Yes," said Ben. He turned to Colin and said softly, "Your mother was such a pretty, young thing.

42
00:03:09.390 --> 00:03:17.634
She said to me once, 'Ben, if I'm ever ill, or if I go away, you must take care of my roses.'

43
00:03:17.635 --> 00:03:23.609
When she did go away, the orders were that no one was ever to come near the garden."

44
00:03:23.610 --> 00:03:26.736
Ben paused to collect his emotions.

45
00:03:26.737 --> 00:03:33.951
Then he said in a strong voice, "But I came over the wall because she gave her orders first."

46
00:03:33.952 --> 00:03:40.146
"I'm glad you did," said Colin. "You will know how to keep our secret."

47
00:03:40.147 --> 00:03:45.378
Earlier in the afternoon, Mary had dropped her trowel on the ground where they were sitting.

48
00:03:45.379 --> 00:03:48.806
Now Colin reached out and picked it up.

49
00:03:48.807 --> 00:03:52.630
He drove the end of the trowel into the dirt.

50
00:03:52.631 --> 00:03:56.268
"You can do it!" Mary said to herself.

51
00:03:56.269 --> 00:04:01.626
Sure enough, Colin managed to turn a few trowels full of dirt.

52
00:04:01.627 --> 00:04:06.040
"You said you'd have me walking and digging," Colin said to Dickon.

53
00:04:06.041 --> 00:04:09.104
"I thought you were saying that just to please me.

54
00:04:09.105 --> 00:04:12.156
But here it's only the first day, and I've already walked.

55
00:04:12.157 --> 00:04:14.661
And now I'm digging!"

56
00:04:14.662 --> 00:04:18.436
"How would you like to plant something?" asked Ben.

57
00:04:18.437 --> 00:04:21.484
"I can get you a rose from the greenhouse."

58
00:04:21.485 --> 00:04:29.524
"Go and get it quickly!" Colin began to dig excitedly, but he wasn't strong enough to dig a very big hole.

59
00:04:29.525 --> 00:04:33.731
Ben hurried off to get the rose while Dickon made the hole deeper.

60
00:04:33.732 --> 00:04:37.694
Mary ran out of the garden to fetch a watering can.

61
00:04:37.695 --> 00:04:43.868
Soon they were all gathered around Colin. Ben took the rose out of the pot.

62
00:04:43.869 --> 00:04:47.896
"I want to plant it before the sun sets," said Colin.

63
00:04:47.897 --> 00:04:51.752
His hands shook as he put the rose in the ground.

64
00:04:51.753 --> 00:04:55.596
He held it while Ben filled the hole with dirt.

65
00:04:55.597 --> 00:05:00.635
"It's planted!" cried Colin. "And the sun is almost down.

66
00:05:00.636 --> 00:05:05.236
Help me up, Dickon. I want to be standing when it sets.

67
00:05:05.237 --> 00:05:07.468
That's part of the magic."

68
00:05:07.469 --> 00:05:12.893
Dickon helped him to his feet. It had been a strange and lovely afternoon.

69
00:05:12.894 --> 00:05:21.983
And as the sun slipped below the horizon, Colin stood smiling in the secret garden.
